RULES FOR SCREEN AGENTS
  - Read data with useApi<T>("/path?query") (key = API path relative to /api) or api.<fn>() for mutations.
    After a mutation call invalidate("/prefix"). SSE events already invalidate the matching prefixes.
  - Open an item in the viewport: const { openItem } = useItem(); openItem("acme-api:commit:abc123").
  - Toasts only after a user action: toast("T-12 → review") / toast(msg, { error: true }).
  - Mode: useStore(s => s.mode) === "readout" -> no hover, no selection, no controls (see 02-ui-spec §4).
  - Range 7|30: useStore(s => s.range), setRange(r).  Search dim on Home: useStore(s => s.searchLit).
  - Font weight 400 only, no italics, no bold (a test scans every .css file under app/). Use the CSS tokens.
  - One global keydown listener lives in app/lib/shortcuts.ts (installed by the shell). Do not add your own
    global listeners. For Esc, call useEscapeLayer("search" | "day" | "viewport", isOpen, close) so it
    joins the order search -> selected day -> viewport. Other keys: put handlers on your own elements.
  - Route containers that mount a child use class "dr-mount" (grid minmax(0,1fr)) so the child fills them.
  - Tests: put *.test.tsx next to your code; MSW answers /api from the fixtures automatically.
    Render with a router: see app/components/shell/shell.test.tsx for the renderApp() helper in test/render.tsx.
